1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,738
BRAMBLE: Case open!

2
00:00:01,738 --> 00:00:04,916
OTTO: Oh no! Mud on Mabel's new sign!

3
00:00:05,116 --> 00:00:08,052
IVY: Now we can't read the name.

4
00:00:08,452 --> 00:00:12,387
Today's case: the name on a muddy sign.

5
00:00:12,787 --> 00:00:16,305
OTTO: S. H. O. P. Suh-huh-op!

6
00:00:16,705 --> 00:00:19,353
BRAMBLE: What does the sign say?

7
00:00:19,753 --> 00:00:22,863
Two letters can make one sound.

8
00:00:23,263 --> 00:00:26,029
S and h make sh.

9
00:00:26,429 --> 00:00:28,596
Sh. Op.

10
00:00:29,196 --> 00:00:30,252
Shop!

11
00:00:30,652 --> 00:00:32,670
It's B! Shop.

12
00:00:33,070 --> 00:00:36,645
Sh is one sound. One line.

13
00:00:37,045 --> 00:00:40,353
O and p. Two dots.

14
00:00:40,753 --> 00:00:43,810
Four letters. Three sounds.

15
00:00:44,210 --> 00:00:45,560
BRAMBLE: Case solved!

16
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:50,867
Say it with me. Two letters can make one sound.

17
00:00:51,267 --> 00:00:55,004
Next case: the till that won't balance.

